      <data key="d_subtopic">CNNs</data>
      <data key="d_tier">core</data>
      <data key="d_desc">y = x W^T + b; the basic learnable linear transformation, with weight (out_features, in_features) and optional bias (out_features).</data>
      <data key="d6"><y:ShapeNode>
        <y:Geometry height="42.0" width="196.0" x="0.0" y="0.0"/>
        <y:Fill color="#AF9FF4" transparent="false"/>
        <y:BorderStyle color="#222222" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
        <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" textColor="#000000" modelName="internal" modelPosition="c">Linear (affine) layer</y:NodeLabel>
        <y:Shape type="roundrectangle"/>
      </y:ShapeNode></data>
    </node>
    <node id="log-sum-exp-stability">
      <data key="d_label">Log-sum-exp numerical stability trick</data>
      <data key="d_topic">Backprop</data>
      <data key="d_subtopic">Backprop</data>
      <data key="d_tier">core</data>
      <data key="d_desc">Subtract the per-row max from logits before exponentiating to keep exp() in range; standard trick to make softmax/log-softmax numerically stable.</data>
      <data key="d6"><y:ShapeNode>
        <y:Geometry height="42.0" width="280.0" x="0.0" y="0.0"/>
        <y:Fill color="#F49FF2" transparent="false"/>
        <y:BorderStyle color="#222222" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
        <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" textColor="#000000" modelName="internal" modelPosition="c">Log-sum-exp numerical stability trick</y:NodeLabel>
        <y:Shape type="roundrectangle"/>
      </y:ShapeNode></data>
    </node>
    <node id="logical-reduction-any-all">
      <data key="d_label">Boolean reduction via .any()/.all()</data>
      <data key="d_topic">Ray Tracing</data>
      <data key="d_subtopic">Ray Tracing</data>
      <data key="d_tier">core</data>
      <data key="d_desc">`t.any(tensor, dim=...)` returns True along a dimension if at least one element is True; used to collapse a (ray, segment) intersection matrix to a per-ray boolean.</data>
      <data key="d6"><y:ShapeNode>
        <y:Geometry height="42.0" width="280.0" x="0.0" y="0.0"/>
        <y:Fill color="#9FA1F4" transparent="false"/>
        <y:BorderStyle color="#222222" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
        <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" textColor="#000000" modelName="internal" modelPosition="c">Boolean reduction via .any()/.all()</y:NodeLabel>
        <y:Shape type="roundrectangle"/>
      </y:ShapeNode></data>
    </node>
    <node id="matmul-backward-rules">
      <data key="d_label">Backward of 2D matmul</data>
      <data key="d_topic">Backprop</data>
      <data key="d_subtopic">Backprop</data>
      <data key="d_tier">core</data>
      <data key="d_desc">For M = X Y, dL/dX = dL/dM · Y^T and dL/dY = X^T · dL/dM; derived from the chain rule by expressing M_pq = sum_r X_pr Y_rq.</data>
      <data key="d6"><y:ShapeNode>
        <y:Geometry height="42.0" width="196.0" x="0.0" y="0.0"/>
        <y:Fill color="#F49FF2" transparent="false"/>
        <y:BorderStyle color="#222222" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
        <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" textColor="#000000" modelName="internal" modelPosition="c">Backward of 2D matmul</y:NodeLabel>
        <y:Shape type="roundrectangle"/>
      </y:ShapeNode></data>
    </node>
    <node id="maximum-backward-tie-split">
      <data key="d_label">Backward of max with tie-splitting</data>
      <data key="d_topic">Backprop</data>
      <data key="d_subtopic">Backprop</data>
      <data key="d_tier">core</data>
      <data key="d_desc">Backward of max(x,y) wrt x is 1 if x&gt;y, 0 if x&lt;y, 0.5 if x==y (PyTorch convention) so gradients sum to 1; same logic mirrored for y.</data>
      <data key="d6"><y:ShapeNode>
        <y:Geometry height="42.0" width="280.0" x="0.0" y="0.0"/>
        <y:Fill color="#F49FF2" transparent="false"/>
        <y:BorderStyle color="#222222" raised="false" type="line" width="1.0"/>
        <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" textColor="#000000" modelName="internal" modelPosition="c">Backward of max with tie-splitting</y:NodeLabel>
        <y:Shape type="roundrectangle"/>
      </y:ShapeNode></data>
    </node>
    <node id="maxpool2d">
